Falsifies `domain_name_system::proofs::tcp_reassembly_is_total_and_honest`.

The defect: `TcpReply::feed` no longer refuses, inside its copy loop, a reply that announces more
than its buffer holds. The check after the loop still reports the first such piece as
`Overflow`, so a caller that stops there is safe; one that feeds again writes past the buffer.

Expected to fail: a slice index out of bounds, on a first piece announcing more than four bytes and
a second piece that arrives anyway.

**Measured blind before it was recorded.** The harness first fed the second piece only when the
first succeeded, and this diff left it green. It now feeds both whatever the first returned.

diff --git a/crates/domain_name_system/src/lib.rs b/crates/domain_name_system/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/domain_name_system/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/domain_name_system/src/lib.rs
@@ -848,7 +848,6 @@
         while !bytes.is_empty() {
             let limit = match self.wanted() {
                 Some(w) if self.have == w => return Err(Error::Trailing),
-                Some(w) if w > self.buf.len() => return Err(Error::Overflow),
                 Some(w) => w,
                 None => 2.min(self.buf.len()),
             };
